@namespace FormCraft.ForMudBlazor

@* The visible required marker for a file-upload field's own label (#262).

   Lives here rather than inline in each upload component so the single- and multiple-file
   components cannot drift — markup divergence between the two is the failure class this library
   keeps re-filing (#146, #177, #184, #189).

   aria-hidden: the requirement is conveyed programmatically by the Browse button's
   aria-describedby, so announcing "star" here would only duplicate it.

   Two classes on purpose. `mud-input-required` is the semantic class the rest of this suite uses
   for "this field is marked required". `formcraft-required-marker` is FormCraft's own hook, and it
   is the one to select or restyle: MudBlazor's only rule for its class is
   `.mud-input-control.mud-input-required > .mud-input-control-input-container > .mud-input-label::after`,
   which never matches this span, so the asterisk here is a real text node rather than CSS content. *@

<span class="mud-input-required formcraft-required-marker" aria-hidden="true">&nbsp;*</span>
